@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@
+TASK
+
+Tier: Mid. Reason: **not low risk — being wrong is hard to detect.** This defect
+coexisted with 768 passing tests and two passing live proofs because the tests
+themselves supplied the repaint the UI never performs. Correcting it requires
+removing that compensation and proving the corrected assertions actually bite.
+
+Goal:
+Fix BLOCKER 1 of `.harness/reviews/M12-cycle1.md` (read that finding — do not
+work from this summary alone): in `web/src/ui/dom-target.ts`, creating a
+conversation must repaint the UI and leave the new conversation selected, so
+that **Send works immediately afterwards with no further user action**; deleting
+must repaint too. Then remove the manual `handle.render()` calls in the test and
+the live proof that were hiding the defect.
+
+Relevant Requirements:
+M12 criterion 6 (human-attested on the physical iPhone): the user types a
+prompt, taps Send, sees output stream, and can cancel. Today there is **no tap
+sequence** that reaches a state where Send does anything, because
+`selectedConversationId` in `dom-target.ts` is only ever set by `paint()`, and
+nothing repaints after a create.
+
+Acceptance Criteria:
+1. Clicking `[data-testid="create-conversation"]` with a profile selected results
+   in the conversation list being repainted (an `[data-testid="open-conversation"]`
+   button exists for the new conversation) **and** the new conversation being the
+   selected one, without any caller invoking `render()` or `select()` by hand.
+2. Immediately after (1), clicking `[data-testid="send"]` with non-empty text in
+   `[data-testid="prompt-input"]` dispatches `actions.send` for the new
+   conversation id. It must not be a silent no-op.
+3. Clicking `[data-testid="delete-conversation"]` repaints the list (the deleted
+   conversation's buttons are gone). If the deleted conversation was the selected
+   one, selection is cleared.
+4. `test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts` no longer calls `handle.render()` (or
+   any other controller method) to compensate for the UI's failure to repaint
+   after a create or a delete. The test drives the app only through DOM events a
+   user could produce: setting `.value` on an input and dispatching `click`.
+5. `src/host/m12-proof.ts` likewise no longer calls `handle.render()` to make the
+   flow progress after creating a conversation. It must exercise the same taps a
+   user makes. (Its two calls are at lines 109 and 149 — read them; if one is
+   legitimately doing something else, say which in Unresolved Issues rather than
+   deleting it blindly.)
+6. **Bite-check, and report the output.** For each assertion you changed or added
+   under (1)-(3): revert your `dom-target.ts` correction temporarily (keep the
+   test change), run the test, and confirm it FAILS. Then restore the correction
+   and confirm it PASSES. Paste both runs' relevant output into your return. An
+   assertion that passes with the correction reverted is not evidence and must be
+   strengthened until it fails.
+
+Implementation note (the mechanism is decided; do not redesign it):
+
+  Create handler (~line 171). Capture `deps` into a local `d` first, then:
+
+      d.actions.createConversation({ profileId: selectedProfileId })
+        .then((conversation) => {
+          d.controller.render();               // reloads conversations from the store
+          d.controller.select(conversation.id); // selects the new one and repaints
+        })
+        .catch(() => {});
+
+  `MountHandle.render()` reloads `store.loadConversations()` and paints;
+  `select()` sets `selectedConversationId` and paints. Both are needed and in
+  that order.
+
+  **Leave the `.catch(() => {})` swallowing for now, with a comment saying error
+  surfacing is added by the BLOCKER 2 correction.** A separate task (M12-C1T2)
+  replaces every swallowed error in this file. Do not do error surfacing here —
+  you would collide with it.
+
+  Delete handler (~line 225): `deleteConversation` is synchronous. After calling
+  it, if the deleted id equals the currently selected one, call
+  `d.controller.select(null)`; then call `d.controller.render()`.
+
+Relevant Files:
+- web/src/ui/dom-target.ts        (the defect; create handler ~171, delete ~225)
+- web/src/ui/mount.ts             (read-only: render/select semantics)
+- web/src/ui/actions.ts           (read-only: createConversation returns Promise<Conversation>)
+- test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts   (manual render at line 243)
+- test/web/ui/dom-target.test.ts           (existing create/delete dispatch tests)
+- src/host/m12-proof.ts                    (manual renders at lines 109, 149)
+- .harness/reviews/M12-cycle1.md           (BLOCKER 1 — read it)
+
+Files Allowed To Change:
+- web/src/ui/dom-target.ts
+- test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts
+- test/web/ui/dom-target.test.ts
+- src/host/m12-proof.ts
+
+Constraints:
+- Follow existing repository patterns.
+- Do not change unrelated behaviour. In particular do NOT touch the send handler's
+  `.catch`, `web/src/main.ts`, `web/src/ui/view-model.ts`, `web/src/ui/mount.ts`,
+  or `web/public/index.html` — other correction tasks own those.
+- Do not add or change the set of `<section>` or `<ul>` elements in
+  `dom-target.ts`'s root. Some tests select positionally (`sections[2]`,
+  `querySelectorAll("ul")[1]`); changing the document shape breaks them and is
+  explicitly out of scope for this cycle.
+- Do not introduce dependencies. happy-dom is test-only and must never be
+  imported by anything under `web/src/`.
+- Do not weaken tests. Removing a `handle.render()` that compensates for the
+  defect is *strengthening*; deleting an assertion is not.
+
+Tests:
+- bun test test/web/ui/dom-target.test.ts test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts
+- bun test        (full suite; must stay green)
+- bunx tsc --noEmit
+- bun run build
+- bun run proof:m12    (LIVE harness — Ollama is running, do not mock it)
+
+Return:
+- Summary
+- Files changed
+- Tests run
+- Test result
+- Bite-check evidence (the reverted-correction failure output and the restored pass)
+- Unresolved issues
