+TASK
+
+Tier: Cheap. It is clearly specified, bounded to one small file plus a test,
+low risk, and settled by a grep-level assertion.
+
+Goal:
+Fix BLOCKER 3 of `.harness/reviews/M12-cycle1.md` (read that finding):
+`web/public/index.html` combines `viewport-fit=cover` with
+`apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style: black-translucent`, which extends the web
+view under the iOS status bar and home indicator, but its CSS compensates with
+nothing (`body { margin: 0; padding: 1rem; }`). The first element in the rendered
+DOM is the prompt `<textarea>`, so on the installed home-screen app it lands
+under the clock and cannot reliably be tapped. Honour the safe-area insets.
+
+Acceptance Criteria:
+1. `web/public/index.html`'s `body` padding honours the safe-area insets on all
+   four sides, e.g.:
+
+       padding-top: max(1rem, env(safe-area-inset-top));
+       padding-right: max(1rem, env(safe-area-inset-right));
+       padding-bottom: max(1rem, env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
+       padding-left: max(1rem, env(safe-area-inset-left));
+
+   Keep 1rem as the floor so nothing regresses on a device with zero insets.
+   Do not remove `viewport-fit=cover` or the `black-translucent` meta — they are
+   what M10 established for standalone mode; the fix is to compensate for them.
+2. A test asserts this over the **source** `web/public/index.html`, not only
+   `web/dist/`: all four `env(safe-area-inset-*)` values are present in the
+   stylesheet, and each is combined with a non-zero floor.
+3. A test asserts the built output carries it too, if there is already a build
+   test that reads `web/dist/index.html` — extend it rather than adding a new
+   file if a natural home exists. Look at `test/build.test.ts` first.
+4. Bite-check: revert the `index.html` change, run the new assertions, confirm
+   they FAIL; restore, confirm they PASS. Paste both runs into your return.
+
+Relevant Files:
+- web/public/index.html                    (the defect; the <style> block, lines 7-19)
+- test/build.test.ts                       (likely home for the built-output assertion)
+- .harness/reviews/M12-cycle1.md           (BLOCKER 3 — read it)
+
+Files Allowed To Change:
+- web/public/index.html
+- test/build.test.ts
+- one new test file under test/web/ if test/build.test.ts is not a natural home
+
+Constraints:
+- Follow existing repository patterns.
+- Do not change the DOM structure of index.html, the meta tags, the manifest
+  link, or the script tag. CSS only.
+- Do not touch anything under web/src/ or src/host/ — other correction tasks own
+  those files this cycle.
+- Do not introduce dependencies.
+- Do not weaken tests.
+
+Tests:
+- bun run build
+- bun test test/build.test.ts
+- bun test        (full suite; must stay green)
+
+Return:
+- Summary
+- Files changed
+- Tests run
+- Test result
+- Bite-check evidence (reverted failure output, restored pass)
+- Unresolved issues
