+TASK
+
+Tier: Cheap. Clearly specified, bounded to three files, low risk, and settled
+outright by `bun run proof:m12` plus the full suite.
+
+Goal:
+The BLOCKER 2 correction appended a new `noticeSection` as the last `<section>`
+in `web/src/ui/dom-target.ts`. Three places in `src/host/m12-proof.ts` locate the
+status region **positionally** as the last section, so they now read the (empty)
+notice section instead of status, and `bun run proof:m12` times out waiting for a
+completion that already happened. Replace positional status lookup with an
+explicit test id, everywhere it is used.
+
+This is the case `.harness/reviews/M12-cycle1.md` sanctions under "Not in scope
+for this cycle": positional DOM selection is a logged follow-up **unless a
+correction forces the document shape to change**, which it did. Fix only the
+selectors that change broke. Do not go hunting for other positional selectors.
+
+Acceptance Criteria:
+1. `web/src/ui/dom-target.ts`'s `statusSection` carries
+   `data-testid="status"` (set with `setAttribute`, matching how the other
+   test ids in that file are set). This adds an attribute only -- it must NOT
+   add, remove or reorder any element, so no positional index anywhere changes.
+2. `src/host/m12-proof.ts` reads the status region via
+   `[data-testid="status"]` in all three places that currently use
+   `sections[sections.length - 1]` (two occurrences) or
+   `section:last-of-type` (one occurrence). Grep the file to find them all --
+   do not trust that count if you find more.
+3. `test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts` currently reads status as
+   `statusSections[statusSections.length - 2]` -- an index the BLOCKER 2
+   correction had to introduce precisely because the shape changed. Change it to
+   select `[data-testid="status"]` too, and update the comment above it.
+4. `bun run proof:m12` PASSES against the LIVE harness (Ollama is running; do not
+   mock it, do not stub it, do not shorten its timeout to make it pass). Paste
+   its last ~15 lines.
+5. `bun test` is green (it was 783 pass / 0 fail before this task), `bunx tsc
+   --noEmit` is clean, `bun run build` is clean.
+6. Bite-check criterion 1: temporarily remove the `data-testid="status"`
+   attribute, run `bun test test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts`, confirm it
+   FAILS; restore and confirm it PASSES. Paste both.
+
+Relevant Files:
+- web/src/ui/dom-target.ts                  (statusSection is created ~line 70 and appended in root.replaceChildren)
+- src/host/m12-proof.ts                     (the three positional status reads)
+- test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts    (the `length - 2` read)
+
+Files Allowed To Change:
+- web/src/ui/dom-target.ts
+- src/host/m12-proof.ts
+- test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts
+
+Constraints:
+- Attribute only in `dom-target.ts`. Do NOT add, remove, reorder or restructure
+  any element; do not touch the create/delete repaint logic, the notice section,
+  the guard-clause notices, or any `.catch` handler. Those are accepted
+  corrections from other tasks.
+- Do not touch any other file. In particular do not touch `web/src/main.ts`,
+  `web/src/ui/mount.ts`, `web/src/ui/view-model.ts`, `web/public/index.html` or
+  `test/build.test.ts`.
+- Do not change `m12-proof.ts` in any way beyond the selector fix -- no new
+  waits, no longer timeouts, no relaxed assertions. If it still fails after the
+  selector fix, that is a real regression: report FAIL and say so rather than
+  making the proof more forgiving.
+- Do not weaken tests.
+- Never run `git stash`, `git checkout --`, `git restore`, `git reset --hard` or
+  `git clean`. This tree holds uncommitted and untracked work from several tasks.
+  To undo your own edit, edit it back by hand.
+
+Tests:
+- bun test test/web/ui/bundle-interactive.test.ts
+- bun test
+- bunx tsc --noEmit
+- bun run build
+- bun run proof:m12    (LIVE)
+
+Return:
+- Summary
+- Files changed
+- Tests run
+- Test result
+- proof:m12 output (last ~15 lines)
+- Bite-check evidence
+- Unresolved issues
